# Census: the dose rows are PRIVATE at contract v3 and must never reach this repo.
# The build writes rows_private.json to a directory outside both repos; these two
# entries are a backstop for a hand-run that pointed --out or --private here.
data/census/dose_latest.json
data/census/rows_private.json
# Report + courtesy-email drafts for Jaden to send by hand; never published.
# EXCEPT the research history below: these dated snapshots are the ONLY record of
# what each county's 911 answer was on a given date. `county_911.json` is overwritten
# by every build and its rows carry no date, so a lost snapshot cannot be rebuilt from
# anything -- unlike the census, whose history is recoverable from BigQuery
# `census.dose_history` and the nightly parquet. Tracked so the record survives.
# Everything else in scratch/ (drafts, caches, raw captures) stays ignored.
!scratch/
scratch/*
!scratch/ems-services/
scratch/ems-services/*
!scratch/ems-services/county_history/
!scratch/ems-services/snapshots/
!scratch/ems-services/history.json
# The two scripts that PRODUCE that history: losing them means the record stops.
!scratch/ems-services/snapshot_counties.py
!scratch/ems-services/county_changes.py
!scratch/ems-services/RESUME_911_MAP.md
!scratch/ems-services/VERIFY_PLAYBOOK.md
!scratch/PLAN_EDITIONS_AND_TIMELINE.md
!scratch/ems-services/VOCABULARY.md

# Unpublished blog draft (not ready to go live) — kept on disk, not deployed
blog/posts/2026-05-19-what-51-ems-protocols-actually-say.html
blog/images/protocol-map-51.svg

